00:19:40,708 --> 00:19:42,469
It's about a hundred residences.

205
00:19:42,509 --> 00:19:43,969
They're all single family homes.

206
00:19:45,049 --> 00:19:58,932
And by my observation, and I think it's fairly accurate, about 15 of those residents are using commercial landscapers, all of whom are unloading, hulking gas,

207
00:20:00,626 --> 00:20:09,793
fueled leaf blowers as a matter of policy and practice at every visit.

208
00:20:11,594 --> 00:20:13,315
But that's about 15%.

209
00:20:14,116 --> 00:20:24,164
And I think that if you take a look at Medford as a whole, I think you're not going to exceed 15%, it's probably less.

210
00:20:25,845 --> 00:20:29,788
But what's happened here is we've reached a tipping point.

211
00:20:30,811 --> 00:20:39,375
At some point, and we have reached it, one of the other speakers indicated that there's been an exponential increase in the use of these devices.

212
00:20:40,696 --> 00:20:42,097
I would call it a metastasis.

213
00:20:42,837 --> 00:20:49,040
I've been here for eight years, and when I first came here, we'd see a leaf blower once in a while through a landscaper.

214
00:20:49,881 --> 00:20:51,982
It's horrendous now.

215
00:20:53,062 --> 00:20:58,125
A couple of weeks ago, and I called this to the attention of the president and to the mayor,

216
00:20:59,110 --> 00:21:00,371
and to another city councilor.

217
00:21:01,552 --> 00:21:14,082
We had one company who has three clients in nearly proximate to my home, show up at 7.15 in the morning.

218
00:21:14,943 --> 00:21:16,744
They didn't leave the neighborhood until 12.15.

219
00:21:16,804 --> 00:21:18,766
They were there for five hours.

220
00:21:20,027 --> 00:21:25,992
And they had four gas leaf blowers going on every property.

221
00:21:28,202 --> 00:21:44,568
And by my calculation, for each hour they had those machines going about 15 minutes, it was about 300 minutes of a single gasoline leaf blower minutes, which is five hours.

222
00:21:44,628 --> 00:21:52,531
And imagine just having one of those machines going for five straight hours and the amount of emissions, the amount of pollutants

223
00:21:53,549 --> 00:22:08,433
the amount of ultrafine particulate, to say nothing of the fact that, you know, all of these ground source contaminants, and this is an issue not only for the gas blowers, but it's an issue for the electric blowers.

224
00:22:08,953 --> 00:22:23,096
This entire concept of shooting ultra high speed air at the ground to clean off your lawn, your driveway, the gutters, the sidewalk, the little nature strip,

225
00:22:24,577 --> 00:22:29,399
That was ill-conceived from the start, you know, and it's become normalized.

226
00:22:29,860 --> 00:22:42,367
But what you've got is, what you're doing is you're aerosolizing, you're dispersing into the public airspace, as well as onto your neighbor's airspace, everything that's on the ground.

227
00:22:43,348 --> 00:22:45,810
in a way that would not normally be done.

228
00:22:46,010 --> 00:22:56,258
And we're talking about mold, we're talking about animal feces and urine, you're talking about fertilizer, pesticides, all kinds of lawn chemicals.

229
00:22:57,059 --> 00:23:08,548
And the fact is, it's much more likely that a resident that's using these commercial landscapers is also going to be applying chemicals to their lawn.

230
00:23:11,685 --> 00:23:27,930
The 85 percenters, including myself and some of the other speakers here, I imagine, are suffering because 15% of the residents require what the landscapers call a polished look.

231
00:23:29,190 --> 00:23:37,353
So that means everything that isn't nailed down on that lawn or your driveway or the street has to be dispersed.

232
00:23:38,033 --> 00:23:39,133
Well, that's just insane.

233
00:23:42,033 --> 00:23:45,134
and we're really being held hostage.

234
00:23:45,955 --> 00:23:59,160
I have seen children on bicycles riding through the streets during one of these visits by the landscapers when they're blowing stuff all over the place, sucking in these pollutants.

235
00:24:00,701 --> 00:24:10,285
What parent in their right mind would take their child out in a baby stroller during one of these visits by these landscapers?

236
00:24:12,398 --> 00:24:30,984
By my calculation, and I've done an informal study and I've provided a list to Madam President and to the mayor, there are more than 50 commercial landscapers plying their trade here in Medford, and they all have multiple clients.

237
00:24:31,465 --> 00:24:41,188
And so it's not just that a landscaper shows up one door, two doors down, they do their job for 45 minutes or an hour and a half and they leave.

238
00:24:42,455 --> 00:24:52,046
What happens is, yeah, they're here, they leave, and just when you think you've gotten some relief, the next commercial landscaper shows up to do somebody else's lawn.

239
00:24:52,346 --> 00:24:53,708
And so this thing just goes on.

240
00:24:53,728 --> 00:24:56,031
I mean, you can have a whole day full of this.

241
00:24:58,678 --> 00:24:59,939
This has to end.

242
00:25:01,540 --> 00:25:18,769
The same arguments against change here were made about lead paint, about asbestos, about seat belts, about catalytic converters, oh, it's gonna be expensive, it's gonna be passed on to the consumer.

243
00:25:21,030 --> 00:25:21,570
We have to be,

244
00:25:26,475 --> 00:25:27,675
sensible about this thing.

245
00:25:27,715 --> 00:25:34,317
This is health, the health of ourselves, the health of our children, the health of babies and infants.

246
00:25:37,618 --> 00:25:42,440
These lawns can be managed without the gas leaf blowers.

247
00:25:42,640 --> 00:25:47,181
They'll find a way, even if they have to combine some use of

248
00:25:48,342 --> 00:25:51,546
electric with adding on another worker.

249
00:25:51,566 --> 00:25:52,747
That's not bad.

250
00:25:52,767 --> 00:25:56,011
Another employee with a rake or a couple of rakes.

251
00:25:56,552 --> 00:26:00,256
You'd be surprised how much improvement there have been in rakes.

252
00:26:00,977 --> 00:26:01,998
I rake my own lawn.

253
00:26:02,018 --> 00:26:02,999
It doesn't take that long.

254
00:26:04,909 --> 00:26:09,251
So other communities have done this across the country.

255
00:26:09,452 --> 00:26:18,137
New York has many communities, Vermont, New Jersey, California, Illinois has a proposal on the table.

256
00:26:18,677 --> 00:26:21,559
Our next door neighbor, it's embarrassing.

257
00:26:22,460 --> 00:26:30,425
They have banned even electric leaf blowers during the non-leaf season.

258
00:26:31,482 --> 00:26:46,415
There is no reason why, at the very minimum, we cannot confine all leaf blowing, electric and or gas, in terms of the residents, to six weeks in the fall,

259
00:26:47,752 --> 00:27:00,657
March 15th to April 30th, and six weeks, that is in the spring, and six weeks in the fall from November 1st, when you have to have some measurable amount of leaves on the ground to December 15th.

260
00:27:01,378 --> 00:27:02,278
That's 12 weeks.

261
00:27:02,498 --> 00:27:04,159
That's actually almost a quarter of the year.

262
00:27:04,879 --> 00:27:12,322
Otherwise, there's absolutely no rationalization for having these air blowers on the ground.

263
00:27:13,078 --> 00:27:17,919
on anybody's property other than for so-called polished look.

264
00:27:18,459 --> 00:27:40,523
But there's no reason that the 85, the super majority of people have to suffer the noise, the toxic emissions and the ground sourced airborne contaminants so that those people who must have that type of a lawn

265
00:27:42,140 --> 00:27:43,820
you know, can be satisfied.

266
00:27:44,221 --> 00:27:45,681
They can still have clean lawns.

267
00:27:46,661 --> 00:27:49,642
They're just going to have to do it in a sensible and a sane way.

268
00:27:50,202 --> 00:27:54,444
I took a look, and I'm only going to take another moment.

