Yeah.

330
00:33:52,359 --> 00:34:08,146
I think what's generally done in other communities is they have carved out an exception for the DPW because they're dealing with very large parcels and they have a tremendous, you know, they have a very large inventory of equipment.

331
00:34:08,406 --> 00:34:12,188
And it's really a question of giving them just enough time to transition to

332
00:34:12,850 --> 00:34:15,613
either battery or electric powered devices.

333
00:34:16,333 --> 00:34:20,537
And also to try as best they can just to minimize the use.

334
00:34:21,678 --> 00:34:26,543
I mean, there's ways that they can even minimize the use of their gas equipment.

335
00:34:27,704 --> 00:34:38,133
But I think in the main, the residents that are suffering, they're suffering in the neighborhoods, not because they, you know,

336
00:34:39,354 --> 00:34:47,161
My child goes to play tennis at Playstead Park or Victory Park or McNally at softball.

337
00:34:48,182 --> 00:34:49,564
The leaf blowers are not out there.

338
00:34:50,504 --> 00:34:55,169
It's here in the communities, here in the neighborhoods that we're seeing the most use.

339
00:34:56,988 --> 00:35:10,477
I don't really have a problem, you know, with having an exception for the DPW, so long as the DPW is going to make a good faith effort to transition to non-lethal, you know,

340
00:35:13,583 --> 00:35:14,103
machinery.

341
00:35:14,944 --> 00:35:15,964
And I think that's possible.

342
00:35:16,904 --> 00:35:18,625
I mean, that's the way the country's going anyway.

343
00:35:18,965 --> 00:35:31,129
I mean, you know, 10 years, 15 years from now, you're not going to see any of these gasoline lawn machines at all.

344
00:35:31,169 --> 00:35:32,169
They just won't be sold.

345
00:35:32,189 --> 00:35:33,770
You know, we're going to electric cars.

346
00:35:34,230 --> 00:35:36,030
But in the meantime, we need relief now.

347
00:35:36,490 --> 00:35:38,571
So, you know, we got to do the best we can.

