600
01:00:43,213 --> 01:00:54,863
And I absolutely do hear the residents that want to see more or, or more limited dates, I think, just knowing that this is an ongoing conversation that this will move to a committee of the whole if motion to do so.

601
01:00:54,883 --> 01:00:54,943
And

602
01:00:55,995 --> 01:00:57,756
I think with a lot of things.

603
01:00:58,256 --> 01:01:15,942
It's just important that that folks have a chance to learn about something before it starts to really move so I think keeping with this draft is a good idea to just keep the conversation going around this so that folks who may not be here tonight may not have, you know, may have missed the notice for this meeting.

604
01:01:16,765 --> 01:01:20,066
We'll have time to look at this and think about this coming for the committee of the whole.

605
01:01:20,146 --> 01:01:26,887
And then again, we can entertain, you know, many more suggestions, make edits and keep this process going.

606
01:01:26,947 --> 01:01:33,028
I think just, you know, keeping a space document and also having the minutes from this meeting that include every single suggestion.

607
01:01:33,168 --> 01:01:36,709
And I will share, Norman, I will share your memorandum with the other counselors.

608
01:01:37,289 --> 01:01:41,070
And of course people can continue to send things and attend meetings.

609
01:01:42,466 --> 01:01:43,426
going back to you, Norman.

610
01:01:43,806 --> 01:01:44,707
Sorry, Councilor Scarpelli.

611
01:01:45,067 --> 01:01:56,789
I would make the motion that we report this out to the Committee of the Whole favorably at this point so we can continue the dialogue and get the input of our fellow colleagues.

612
01:01:56,969 --> 01:02:11,172
And like you said, Council President, as the word gets out, then I'm sure we'll be getting the phone calls and the emails from the business owners that own landscape companies in Medford

613
01:02:11,672 --> 01:02:24,285
they can share their concerns or their, you know, and that's something that we can entertain and listen and, you know, and have that dialogue in a bigger forum.

614
01:02:24,786 --> 01:02:28,570
But like I said, I think this is a good starting off point.

615
01:02:28,650 --> 01:02:32,114
I think that, you know, having Mr. Moki has been

616
01:02:32,855 --> 01:02:35,038
always been the voice of reason.

617
01:02:35,479 --> 01:02:44,472
Um, you know, you always find find yourself when your question, you listen to Mr Mulkey because he's always, um, he's always in the middle.

618
01:02:44,933 --> 01:02:47,256
I don't think Mr Mulkey is taking the side he's doing with you.

619
01:02:47,837 --> 01:02:49,018
what's best for our community.

620
01:02:49,278 --> 01:02:53,502
And it's refreshing and I appreciate all his hard work.

621
01:02:53,582 --> 01:03:07,054
And again, obviously Norman didn't do much work to prepare, but it's good to hear, like I said, when you have educated constituents sharing their input.

622
01:03:07,694 --> 01:03:10,597
And these are concerns that we hear.

623
01:03:10,657 --> 01:03:14,040
I mean, I had a neighbor come to me just the other day for a neighbor that was,

624
01:03:14,680 --> 01:03:22,827
doing work and their concrete company was using the blowers and they understood that they started doing that.

625
01:03:22,847 --> 01:03:27,932
I went over and I talked to the gentleman and I said, listen, could you at least start doing this when people are at work?

626
01:03:28,533 --> 01:03:30,234
And they agreed.

627
01:03:30,314 --> 01:03:34,438
But once it's out there and all permits

628
01:03:35,068 --> 01:03:38,090
and that is out there in ink.

629
01:03:38,370 --> 01:03:40,612
I think it's important that they'll know that.

630
01:03:40,672 --> 01:03:42,353
So again, thank you.

631
01:03:42,653 --> 01:03:46,295
And I'll make that motion to move forward favorably to the committee of the whole.

632
01:03:46,796 --> 01:03:47,296
And I would second.

633
01:03:47,316 --> 01:03:48,117
Thank you, Councilor Scarpelli.

634
01:03:48,657 --> 01:03:54,681
On the motion of Councilor Scarpelli to report the paper out favorably to committee of the whole, seconded by Councilor Sang.

635
01:03:55,241 --> 01:03:56,642
Mr. Clerk, if you could please call the roll.

636
01:03:57,162 --> 01:03:58,023
Councilor Scarpelli.

637
01:04:00,625 --> 01:04:00,885
Yes.

638
01:04:01,505 --> 01:04:02,186
Councilor Sang.

639
01:04:02,666 --> 01:04:02,886
Yes.

640
01:04:03,346 --> 01:04:03,947
President Morrell.

641
01:04:04,938 --> 01:04:08,359
Yes, three in the affirmative, zero in the negative, the motion passes.

642
01:04:09,380 --> 01:04:14,201
Mr. Kaplan, if you could, if you want to take us out, if you could be brief as you've had.

643
01:04:14,301 --> 01:04:17,362
I had a feeling you were going to say that.

644
01:04:18,463 --> 01:04:20,964
Mr. Scapelli, you took the words right out of my mouth.

645
01:04:21,064 --> 01:04:26,726
There's an old adage, to a man with a hammer, everything looks like a nail.

646
01:04:27,906 --> 01:04:39,053
and you know we're finding the masons are using the leaf blowers and we're finding the fellas up on the ladders cleaning gutters they're using the gasoline blowers too.

647
01:04:41,115 --> 01:04:48,300
I just want to conclude by urging the council to look at

648
01:04:49,383 --> 01:04:51,765
at passing the strongest possible ordinance.

649
01:04:52,425 --> 01:04:57,488
Because as a practical matter, we only have one chance to get this right.

650
01:04:58,288 --> 01:05:02,231
Whatever ordinance is passed, we're going to be stuck with.

651
01:05:02,251 --> 01:05:07,234
This isn't going to be an annual revisitation of this ordinance.

652
01:05:07,554 --> 01:05:09,255
We've got to get it right the first time.

653
01:05:09,495 --> 01:05:17,080
And I think as far as the landscapers giving them additional time

654
01:05:18,488 --> 01:05:19,228
or roll it out.

655
01:05:21,190 --> 01:05:31,678
If they don't understand where the wind is blowing here, if they don't understand the groundswell movement against these machines, then they are willfully blind.

656
01:05:32,659 --> 01:05:35,742
The Globe just did a survey and a poll.

657
01:05:36,282 --> 01:05:46,931
They had an argument section a couple of weeks ago, and the poll is running 72% in favor of banning gasoline leaf blowers.

658
01:05:47,531 --> 01:05:50,974
And if you take a look at next door, you'll see a lot of comments there.

659
01:05:51,334 --> 01:05:54,576
I mean, it's everywhere in the public forum.

660
01:05:54,696 --> 01:06:01,782
So I don't really have any sympathy for the landscape of saying, well, this is catching us by surprise.

661
01:06:02,082 --> 01:06:07,186
It can't be catching them by surprise unless they have their head in the ground.

662
01:06:07,726 --> 01:06:09,467
Well, thank you very much.

663
01:06:09,587 --> 01:06:10,828
Thank you very much, Madam President.

664
01:06:11,469 --> 01:06:12,269
Thank you, Mr. Kaplan.

665
01:06:13,570 --> 01:06:14,171
Councilor Scarpelli.

666
01:06:15,693 --> 01:06:16,714
Okay, I just saw you on mute.

667
01:06:17,294 --> 01:06:18,555
Nope, motion to adjourn, it's off.

668
01:06:19,336 --> 01:06:21,617
On the motion of Councilor Scarpelli to adjourn.

669
01:06:22,258 --> 01:06:24,359
Seconded by... Second.

670
01:06:24,880 --> 01:06:26,501
Councilor Sviggum, the only person who can second.

671
01:06:28,302 --> 01:06:31,044
And I do just want to thank you, Commissioner Moki, for taking the time to be out here.

672
01:06:31,084 --> 01:06:35,007
I know we tend to bring you to a lot of these things and put a lot on your department.

673
01:06:35,847 --> 01:06:40,851
And I think we've spoken in past meetings about the need for more code enforcement folks.

674
01:06:42,143 --> 01:06:44,204
I'm sure we'll all be speaking to that very soon.

675
01:06:44,224 --> 01:06:48,886
You're welcome.

676
01:06:49,406 --> 01:06:50,686
Mr. Clerk, if you could please call the roll.

677
01:06:52,027 --> 01:06:52,807
Councilor Scarpelli.

678
01:06:53,427 --> 01:06:53,728
Yes.

679
01:06:54,128 --> 01:06:54,688
Councilor Hussain.

680
01:06:55,108 --> 01:06:55,568
Yes.

681
01:06:56,169 --> 01:06:56,769
President Morrell.

682
01:06:57,389 --> 01:06:57,609
Yes.

683
01:06:58,009 --> 01:06:59,430
Three in the affirmative, zero in the negative.

684
01:06:59,450 --> 01:07:01,150
The motion passes and the meeting is adjourned.

685
01:07:02,031 --> 01:07:03,491
Good night, everyone.

686
01:07:03,511 --> 01:07:04,192
Good night, everyone.

687
01:07:04,272 --> 01:07:04,552
Thank you.

